-- title:
--   Generic restriction of a global 1-form factors through the cusp stalk
-- statement:
--   Write $R =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to the prime $p$, and $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, $\bar F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` for the $\mathbb{Q}$- resp. $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid N$. Fixed are: $N \neq 0$ with $p \nmid N$; an embedding $\iota_0 : \bar{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathbb{C}$; an integral scheme $X$ with a proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ morphism $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and a cover $\mathcal{V}$ of $X$ by two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with affine intersection; a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with function field $F_N$ together with an isomorphism $e_0$ onto the fibre $X_{\mathbb{Q}}$ over the structure maps, the generic point of $M_0.C$ lying in the preimage of $U_0$; a ring homomorphism $\iota : \Gamma(X, U_0) \to \bar F_N$ which, by `hιdef`, sends $a$ to the coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ of the element of $F_N$ corresponding under $M_0$'s function-field identification to the germ of $a$ at the generic point, and which by `hιR` restricts on $R$ to $R \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}} \to \bar F_N$; an additive map $\mathrm{res}$ from the global Čech $0$-cocycles $H^0$ of the Kähler sections of $\mathcal{V}$ (the kernel of the difference map $\Omega_{\Gamma(X,U_0)/R} \times \Omega_{\Gamma(X,U_1)/R} \to \Omega_{\Gamma(X,U_0 \cap U_1)/R}$) to $\Omega_{\bar F_N/\bar{\mathbb{Q}}}$, given by functoriality of Kähler differentials along $(R \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}, \iota)$ applied to the $U_0$-component; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$ and a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the $q$-adic cusp `cuspInftyFull N`, matched by a $\mathbb{Q}$-point $y$ of $X_{\mathbb{Q}}$ which factors through $\varepsilon_\infty$ and maps to $x_0$ under $e_0^{-1}$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field $\bar F_N$ identified with the fibre $X_{\bar{\mathbb{Q}}}$, whose place assignment is Galois-equivariant for the coefficientwise action `arithmeticGalois` (`hgal`) and compatible with $M_0$ under pullback of valuation subrings along $F_N \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} F_N \cong \bar F_N$ (`hcompat`); for every valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p \in A$ nonunit, a lift $\rho_A : R \to A$ of $R \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, a curve model $M_A$ over the residue field of $A$ with function field `modularFunctionFieldFullC` identified with the corresponding fibre of $c$, and, when that residue field is algebraically closed, a place-reduction map $r$ in the sense of `IsPlaceReductionModL` compatible with the specialisation of points (`hsp`). Finally let $s$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ with $\{s\}$ closed such that the image of $x_0$ in $X$ specialises to $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$, and let $\omega \in H^0$. Giving the stalk $S = \mathcal{O}_{X, \varepsilon_\infty(s)}$ its $R$-algebra structure through the global structure map of $c$, the assertion is that there exist $\omega_s \in \Omega_{S/R}$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{Exp} : S \to \bar F_N$ restricting on $R$ to $R \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}} \to \bar F_N$ such that, firstly, for every $z \in S$ the image $\mathrm{Exp}(z)$ in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the element of $F_N$ obtained from $z$ by specialising to the stalk at the image of $x_0$, pulling back along $e_0$ to $\mathcal{O}_{M_0.C, x_0}$, passing to the function field and applying $M_0$'s identification backwards; and secondly $\mathrm{res}\,\omega$ is the image of $\omega_s$ under the map of Kähler differentials induced by $(R \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}, \mathrm{Exp})$.
--
--   This is the stalk-level form of the $q$-expansion description of the chart map: it moves the defining identity for $\iota$ from the generic point to the stalk of the cuspidal section at the closed point $s$ of $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, and records that the generic restriction of a global relative $1$-form on the model $X$ factors through that stalk. It is used in the integral $q$-expansion comparison for $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, namely in the two statements expressing the $q$-expansion of a global differential as the image of a power series.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_kaehlerDifferential_stalk_and_ringHom_res_eq_mapOfRingHom_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero.lean

